What is the difference between a rocket and a spaceship?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A rocket is a vehicle that is designed to travel through space, while a spaceship is a spacecraft that is designed to carry people or cargo from one place to another in space. Rockets are used to launch spacecraft into orbit, whereas spaceships are used to transport astronauts and equipment to and from space. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How long does it take for a spacecraft to reach Mars?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The time it takes for a spacecraft to reach Mars depends on a number of factors, including the relative positions of Earth and Mars at the time of launch, the speed of the spacecraft, and the trajectory it follows. In general, it can take anywhere from six to eight months for a spacecraft to travel from Earth to Mars. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you explain how a rocket engine works?
<|end|>
