What SQL query can be used to retrieve data on customer purchases, including the products they bought, the emotional state they were in at the time of purchase, and any external factors that may have influenced their decision to buy? The table "purchases" contains columns for customer ID, product ID, purchase date, emotional state, and external influence.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To retrieve data on customer purchases, including the products they bought, the emotional state they were in at the time of purchase, and any external factors that may have influenced their decision to buy, you can use the following SQL query:
```
SELECT purchases.customer_id, products.product_name, purchases.purchase_date, <|fim_suf|>, purchases.external_influence
FROM purchases
JOIN products ON purchases.product_id = products.product_id;
```
This query joins the "purchases" table with the "products" table using the product ID column. It selects the customer ID, product name, purchase date, emotional state, and external influence columns from the "purchases" table. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
