How can I calculate the square root of a number with precision up to the hundredth decimal place in Scala? Can you provide an example of calculating the square root of 156 using the Babylonian method? Also, can you compare the result with the built-in Scala function?
Here's an example of computing the square root of 156 using the Babylonian method in Scala:
def babylonianMethod(n: Double): Double = {
 var x = n
 var y = 1.0
 val precision = 0.000001
 while (x - y > precision) {
 x = (x + y) / 2
 y = n / x
 }
 BigDecimal(x).setScale(100, BigDecimal.RoundingMode.HALF_UP).toDouble
}
val sqrt156 = babylonianMethod(156)
println(sqrt156)
And here's how you can calculate the square root of 156 using the built-in Scala function:
val sqrt156 = math.sqrt(156)
println(sqrt156)
You can compare the results of both methods to check their accuracy.
<|end|>
