Can you explain the concept of time dilation in simple terms?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Time dilation refers to the difference in time intervals measured by two observers in relative motion. In simpler terms, if there are two people moving at different speeds, they may experience time differently. The faster someone is moving, the slower time passes for them compared to someone who is stationary. This effect has been observed and measured in experiments involving high speed particles. <|endoftext|>
