<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here are the steps you can follow to sort the table and extract the top five records based on surface area:
1. Open the Excel file containing the table of lakes.
2. Click on the cell containing the first column header (e.g. "Lake Name") to select the entire column.
3. Hold down the Shift key and click on the cell containing the surface area column header to select both columns.
4. Click on the "Data" tab in the top menu, then click on "Sort."
5. In the "Sort" dialog box, <|fim_suf|>, with the largest lakes at the top.
8. To extract the top five records based on surface area, simply select the first five rows of the table (excluding the header row) and copy them to a new sheet or location in the same sheet.
That's it! You should now have a list of the five biggest lakes in the United States based on surface area. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
