<|end|>
<|asst|>
Definitely! Here are the steps to create a chart or graph that shows the size of each lake relative to the others:
1. Select the cells containing the lake names and their corresponding surface areas.
2. Click on the "Insert" tab in the top menu, then choose the type of chart or graph you want to create (e.g. bar chart, pie chart, etc.).
3. Excel will automatically create a chart using the selected data. You can customize the chart by adding titles, labels, and other formatting options as needed.
4. To make the chart show the size of each lake relative to the others, you can change the chart type to a 100% stacked chart. This will show each lake's surface area as a percentage of the total surface area of all the lakes in the dataset.
5. You can further customize the chart by adding colors, legends, and other visual elements to make it more visually appealing and informative.
That's it! With these steps, you should be able to create a chart or graph that shows the size of each lake relative to the others in your dataset. <|endoftext|>
