<|asst|>
Inflation refers to a sustained increase in the general level of prices for goods and services in an economy. It can lead to a decrease in the purchasing power of money, as people need to spend more to buy the same amount of goods and services. This, in turn, can lead to a decrease in consumer spending, which can have a negative impact on businesses. It can also lead to an increase in interest rates, which can make borrowing more expensive for businesses and individuals alike. <|endoftext|>
