1. Select the cell where you want to display the total quantity.
2. Type the equal sign (=) to begin the formula.
3. Click on the cell containing the first quantity value.
4. Type a plus sign (+).
5. Click on the cell containing the second quantity value.
6. Continue this process for all the quantity values in the table.
7. Type the closing parenthesis to complete the formula.
8. Press Enter to display the total.

The formula should look like this:
=SUM(B2:B10)

This will add up all the quantity values in cells B2 through B10 and display the total in the selected cell. <|endoftext|>
