matches = {};
% Loop through each word in the dictionary
for i = 1:length(dictionary)
 word = dictionary{i};
 
 % Check if the word starts with "s" and ends with "weet"
 if startsWith(word, 's') && endsWith(word, 'weet')
 matches = [matches, word]; % Add the word to the matches array
 end
end
% Display the matching words
disp(matches);
```
This code defines the dictionary as a cell array of strings and initializes an empty array to store the matching words. It then loops through each word in the dictionary and checks if it starts with "s" and ends with "weet". If a word matches these criteria, it is added to the matches array. Finally, the code displays the matching words. <|endoftext|>
