Can you explain how the shuffling of the interests list works in this code?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Certainly! In this code, the interests list is shuffled using a Fisher-Yates shuffle algorithm. This algorithm works by iterating through the list from the last index down to the first index and swapping each element with a randomly chosen element that comes before it. 
In this case, the `OrderBy` method is used to sort the interests list by a randomly generated number for each element, effectively shuffling the list in place. This ensures that the interests are randomized and not repeated in any of the product ideas. <|endoftext|>
