How does the Android operating system differ from iOS?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Android is an open-source operating system developed by Google, while iOS is a closed operating system developed by Apple. This means that Android is more customizable and allows for greater flexibility in terms of app development and device customization, while iOS is more secure and streamlined. Android also has a wider range of devices available at varying price points, while iOS is only available on Apple devices. <|endoftext|>
