Can you explain what a ROM is in relation to Android devices?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A ROM, or Read-Only Memory, is a version of the Android operating system that has been modified by developers to include additional features and customization options. Custom ROMs can be installed by users who have rooted their devices, and can offer benefits such as improved performance and battery life, as well as access to features that are not available on stock Android. However, installing custom ROMs can also void the device's warranty and should be done with caution. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
