You can use the `reverse` function from the `algorithm` library in C++. Here's an example:

```
#include 
#include 
#include 

using namespace std;

int main() {
 string str = "Hello, world!";
 reverse(str.begin(), str.end());
 cout << str << endl;
 return 0;
}

// Output: "!dlrow ,olleH"
