How can I generate a table with the names of 5 vegetables belonging to the order Brassicales and starting with the letter 'C', along with their respective vitamin contents and recommended daily intake values for adults, using R code? 
Here is an example code that can achieve this:
```R
library(dplyr)
# create a data frame with the vegetable names, vitamin content, and recommended daily intake values
veggies <- data.frame(
 name = c("Cabbage", "Cauliflower", "Collard Greens", "Chinese Broccoli", "Choy Sum"),
 vitamin_content = c("Vitamin C: 36.6mg, Vitamin K: 76μg", "Vitamin C: 48.2mg, Vitamin K: 16μg", 
 "Vitamin C: 35mg, Vitamin K: 440μg", "Vitamin C: 79mg, Vitamin K: 105μg", 
 "Vitamin C: 36mg, Vitamin K: 98μg"),
 recommended_intake = rep("90g", 5)
)
# filter the vegetables belonging to the order Brassicales and starting with the letter 'C'
brassicales_veggies <- veggies %>%
 filter(grepl("^C", name)) 
# create a table with the filtered vegetables and their respective vitamin contents and recommended daily intake values
table <- knitr::kable(brassicales_veggies, format = "html", 
 col.names = c("Vegetable Name", "Vitamin Content (per 100g)", "Recommended Daily Intake for Adults (in grams)"))
# print the table
cat(table)
```
<|end|>
