While both genres aim to scare and thrill the audience, there are some differences between them. Thrillers are usually more focused on suspense and anticipation, while horror movies tend to focus on gore and violence. Thriller films typically have a protagonist who is trying to stop a dangerous person or group, whereas horror movies often involve a group of people trying to survive against an evil force. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What is the most successful horror movie of all time?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
There have been many successful horror movies over the years, but according to Box Office Mojo, the highest-grossing horror movie of all time is "It" (2017), directed by Andy Muschietti. The film, which is based on the Stephen King novel of the same name, grossed over $700 million worldwide. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Are there any psychological benefits to watching horror movies?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
While some people might find horror movies unpleasant or disturbing, studies have shown that watching horror films can actually provide some psychological benefits. For example, they can help people confront their fears and anxieties in a safe and controlled environment. They can also stimulate feelings of excitement and adrenaline, which can be enjoyable for some viewers. Additionally, some people find that watching horror movies can help them feel more connected to others, as it provides a shared experience that can be discussed and analyzed with friends or family members. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




