Certainly! You can use the `sort` function in MATLAB to perform a lexicographic sort on a cell array consisting of strings. Here's an example code snippet that sorts the `words` cell array in alphabetical order:
```
words = {'journalism', 'politics', 'law'};
sorted_words = sort(words)
```
The output of this code will be:
```
sorted_words = 
 'journalism' 'law' 'politics'
```
If you want to sort the cell array in descending order, you can use the `'descend'` option:
```
sorted_words_desc = sort(words, 'descend')
```
The output of this code will be:
```
sorted_words_desc = 
 'politics' 'law' 'journalism'
```
I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions. <|endoftext|>
