Can you explain the concept of dark matter?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Dark matter is a hypothetical form of matter that is thought to make up approximately 85% of the matter in the universe. It does not emit, absorb, or reflect light, which makes it invisible to telescopes and other instruments that detect electromagnetic radiation. The existence of dark matter is inferred from its gravitational effects on visible matter, such as stars and galaxies, and from the cosmic microwave background radiation. Despite many years of study, the nature of dark matter remains unknown, and it is one of the biggest mysteries in astrophysics today. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


