How can I retrieve a list of all orders and their corresponding customer names and product details using an INNER JOIN on multiple tables? I have a table called "orders" with columns such as order_id, customer_id, and item_id, a table called "customers" with columns such as customer_id and name, and a table called "items" with columns such as item_id and product_details. Can you provide an example SQL query using INNER JOIN to achieve this? 
[JSON data] 
{
 "orders": [
 {
 "order_id": 1,
 "customer_id": 1,
 "item_id": 1
 },
 {
 "order_id": 2,
 "customer_id": 2,
 "item_id": 3
 },
 {
 "order_id": 3,
 "customer_id": 1,
 "item_id": 2
 }
 ],
 "customers": [
 {
 "customer_id": 1,
 "name": "John Smith"
 },
 {
 "customer_id": 2,
 "name": "Jane Doe"
 }
 ],
 "items": [
 {
 "item_id": 1,
 "product_details": "Product A"
 },
 {
 "item_id": 2,
 "product_details": "Product B"
 },
 {
 "item_id": 3,
 "product_details": "Product C"
 }
 ]
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Certainly! Here's an example SQL query that retrieves a list of all orders and their corresponding customer names and product details using INNER JOIN on the "orders", "customers", and "items" tables:
```
SELECT o.order_id, c.name AS customer_name, i.product_details
FROM orders o
INNER JOIN customers c ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id
INNER JOIN items i ON o.item_id = i.item_id;
```
This query selects the order_id from the "orders" table, the name from the "customers" table (using an alias of "customer_name" for readability), and the product_details from the "items" table. The INNER JOINs are used to join the tables together based on their common columns (customer_id and item_id) to create a single result set with all the desired information.
I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
