How can I add the following items 'Acer laptop, Philips iron, LG refrigerator' to my shopping list using Java code?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a sample Java code that you can use to add the items to your shopping list:
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
public class ShoppingList {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 List shoppingList = new ArrayList<>();
 
 // Add items to the shopping list
 shoppingList.add("Acer laptop");
 shoppingList.add("Philips iron");
 shoppingList.add("LG refrigerator");
 
 // Print the shopping list
 System.out.println("Shopping List:");
 for (String item : shoppingList) {
 System.out.println("- " + item);
 }
 }
}
```
This code creates an empty `ArrayList` named `shoppingList`, and then adds the three items to it using the `add` method. Finally, <|fim_mid|>it prints the shopping list using a `for` loop. You can customize the code to suit your specific needs. <|endoftext|>
