For audio files, you can use the PyDub library, which provides a simple interface for working with audio files in Python. You can use it to extract audio from video files, convert between different audio formats, and apply various effects to audio files.

Finally, if you want to add interactive elements like graphs or charts to your web page, you can use the Plotly library. It provides a user-friendly interface for creating interactive visualizations, and supports a wide range of chart types, from basic line and bar charts to more complex 3D visualizations.

These libraries should help you add some multimedia elements to your web page and make it more engaging for your audience. <|endoftext|>
