How can I write a customized R function that will perform a multi-variable linear regression analysis on a given data frame with categorical and numerical predictor variables? The output will be a detailed summary of the regression analysis including p-values and coefficients for each predictor variable. Can you provide an example of how to use this function to analyze the dataset "mtcars", where "mpg" is the response variable and "wt", "cyl" and "disp" are the predictor variables? The function should also handle missing values and outliers in the dataset appropriately.
[R code]
custom_lin_reg <- function(data, resp_var, pred_vars){
 model <- lm(data[[resp_var]] ~ ., data = data[,c(resp_var,pred_vars)], na.action=na.omit)
 summary(model)
}
#Example usage:
