<|user|>
How does the process of natural selection work?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Natural selection is the process by which certain traits become more or less common in a population over time based on their impact on survival and reproduction. Organisms with advantageous traits are more likely to survive and pass those traits on to their offspring, while those with disadvantageous traits are less likely to survive and reproduce. This leads to changes in the frequency of certain traits within a population over generations. <|endoftext|>
