2. Insertion Sort - This algorithm picks an element from the list and places it in its correct position within a sorted subarray.

3. Selection Sort - This algorithm sorts an array by repeatedly finding the minimum element from unsorted part of the array and putting it at the beginning.

4. Merge Sort - This algorithm divides the input array into two halves, calls itself for the two halves and then merges the two sorted halves.

5. Quick Sort - This algorithm picks an element as pivot and partitions the given array around the picked pivot.

6. Heap Sort - This algorithm uses a binary heap to sort the input array.

These are just a few examples of sorting algorithms. Each has its own strengths and weaknesses, and choosing the right one depends on the specific requirements of the problem at hand. <|endoftext|>
