Sure! Black holes are extremely dense regions of space where the gravitational pull is so strong that nothing, not even light, can escape. They form when massive stars collapse in on themselves, creating a singularity with infinite density and zero volume. Black holes come in different sizes, with the smallest ones being only a few miles across and the largest ones being billions of times more massive than the sun. While black holes cannot be directly observed, their presence can be inferred by observing the effects of their gravity on nearby matter. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
