What is a stored procedure in a database?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A stored procedure is a precompiled set of SQL statements that are stored in a database and can be executed as a single unit. Stored procedures can be used to encapsulate commonly used SQL code or business logic, which can simplify application development and maintenance. Stored procedures can also provide security benefits by allowing access to the underlying data only through the stored procedure, rather than directly accessing the tables. <|endoftext|>
