Can you explain how blockchain works?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Blockchain is a distributed ledger technology that allows multiple parties to maintain a secure and tamper-proof record of transactions without the need for a centralized intermediary. Each block in the chain contains a cryptographic hash of the previous block, along with a timestamp and a batch of new transactions. Once a block is validated by the network, it is added to the chain and becomes part of the permanent record. The decentralized nature of the system makes it difficult for any single actor to manipulate the data or alter the historical record. <|endoftext|>
