Can you explain the concept of quantum entanglement in simple terms?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Quantum entanglement is a phenomenon where two or more particles become linked and their properties become correlated. These particles can be separated by large distances but still exhibit a connection. For example, if two entangled particles are measured to have opposite spins, then measuring one particle will instantly determine the spin of the other particle, regardless of the distance between them. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How do scientists study the behavior of subatomic particles?
<|end|>
