What are the top ten most populous cities in France based on the latest official census data available? Please provide their names in descending order and their corresponding population figures. Additionally, only cities with a population of over one million should be included in the list. Moreover, for each city, please also provide the percentage change in population from the previous census.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Based on the latest official census data available, the top ten most populous cities in France with a population of over one million are:
1. Paris - Population: 2,148,271 (an increase of 4.1% from the previous census)
2. Marseille - Population: 861,635 (an increase of 0.3% from the previous census)
3. Lyon - Population: 515,695 (an increase of 4.2% from the previous census)
4. Toulouse - Population: 479,553 (an increase of 4.9% from the previous census)
5. Nice - Population: 340,017 (an increase of 3.6% from the previous census)
6. Nantes - Population: 309,346 (an increase of 6.4% from the previous census)
7. Strasbourg - Population: 280,966 (an increase of 3.7% from the previous census)
8. Montpellier - Population: 277,639 (an increase of 5.6% from the previous census)
9. Bordeaux - Population: 257,804 (an increase of 7.7% from the previous census)
10. Lille - Population: 232,787 (an increase of 2.2% from the previous census)
Note: These population figures are based on the 2017 census data. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you tell me about the history of the Eiffel Tower?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The Eiffel Tower is a wrought-iron lattice tower located on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It was named after Gustave Eiffel, whose company designed and built the tower as the entrance arch to the 1889 World's Fair. At the time it was built, the tower was the tallest man-made structure in the world, standing at 324 meters (1,063 feet) tall. It held this title until the completion of the Chrysler Building in New York City in 1930. Today, the Eiffel Tower is one of the most recognizable landmarks in the world and attracts millions of visitors each year. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
That's interesting! How long did it take to build the Eiffel Tower?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Construction of the Eiffel Tower began in 1887 and was completed in 1889, just in time for the opening of the World's Fair. The tower was built in two years, two months, and five days, an impressive feat considering the technology available at the time. The tower was built using over 18,000 pieces of wrought iron and almost 2.5 million rivets. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Has the Eiffel Tower always been used as a tourist attraction?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
While the Eiffel Tower was originally built as the entrance arch to the 1889 World's Fair, it quickly became a global icon and a symbol of Paris. In the early 20th century, it was used for scientific experiments in fields such as meteorology, physics, and radio transmissions. During World War I, it served as a crucial communication center for the French military. Today, the Eiffel Tower is primarily a tourist attraction, with visitors from all over the world coming to admire its stunning views and learn about its history. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




<|fim_suf|>}
}
<|end|>
