In this code, we define an array of patterns that are commonly associated with sarcasm, such as "love", "so much fun", "can't wait", etc. We then iterate over each pattern and use the `preg_match` function to check if the pattern appears in the given sentence. If any of the patterns are found, we return `true` to indicate that the sentence is sarcastic. Otherwise, we return `false`.
Note that this is a very simple approach and may not work well for all cases of sarcasm. For more accurate detection, you may want to consider using machine learning algorithms or sentiment analysis libraries such as the Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK) or Stanford CoreNLP. <|endoftext|>
