<|fim_suf|>, the Factory pattern, and the Observer pattern. The MVC pattern separates the application into three interconnected components - the Model (data), the View (user interface), and the Controller (logic). The Singleton pattern ensures that there is only one instance of a class in the system, while the Factory pattern creates objects without exposing the underlying implementation details. The Observer pattern defines a one-to-many relationship between objects such that when one object changes state, all of its dependents are notified and updated automatically. <|endoftext|>
