Here's a puzzle for you! I have some Scala code that I want to modify. I need to calculate sentiment scores for multiple texts and identify the most frequent sentiment words used by the writer in each text. Can you help me figure out how to make these modifications? It's like a puzzle!
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, I can help you with that! Can you please share the Scala code that you have written so far? <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Thank you! Here is the code that I have so far:

```
object SentimentAnalysis {
 def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {
 val texts = Seq(
 "I am so happy today!",
 "I feel sad",
 "This movie is terrible"
 )
 val sentiments = Seq(
 "happy",
 "sad",
 "terrible"
 )

 val sentimentScores = texts.map(text => {
 var score = 0
 sentiments.foreach(sentiment => {
 if (text.toLowerCase.contains(sentiment)) {
 score += 1
 }
 })
 score
 })

 println(sentimentScores)
 }
}
```
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Great, thanks for sharing the code with me! To modify it to identify the most frequent sentiment words used by the writer in each text, you can use a `Map` to keep track of the frequency of each sentiment word in each text. You can then iterate through the `Map` to find the sentiment with the highest frequency for each text. Here's an example of how you can modify your code:

```
object SentimentAnalysis {
 def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {
 val texts = Seq(
 "I am so happy today!",
 "I feel sad",
 "This movie is terrible"
 )
 val sentiments = Seq(
 "happy",
 "sad",
 "terrible"
 )

 val sentimentScores = texts.map(text => {
 var score = 0
 var frequencyMap = scala.collection.mutable.Map[<|fim_suf|>, Int]()
 sentiments.foreach(sentiment => {
 if (text.toLowerCase.contains(sentiment)) {
 score += 1
 if (frequencyMap.contains(sentiment)) {
 frequencyMap(sentiment) += 1
 } else {
 frequencyMap(sentiment) = 1
 }
 }
 })
 val mostFrequentSentiment = frequencyMap.maxBy(_._2)._1
 (score, mostFrequentSentiment)
 })

 println(sentimentScores)
 }
}
```

Let me know if you have any questions or need further help modifying your code! <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


