How can I modify the MATLAB code to generate a password that is 12 characters long and satisfies the following criteria:
- Contains at least two uppercase letters
- Contains at least two lowercase letters
- Contains at least two numbers
- Contains at least two special characters from the following list: !@#$%^&*()_+-=?
Additionally, can you provide a table showing the frequency of each character type in the generated password?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is a modified MATLAB code that generates a password that meets the criteria you specified:
```
passwordLength = 12;
numUppercase = 2;
numLowercase = 2;
numNumbers = 2;
numSpecialChars = 2;
specialChars = '!@#$%^&*()_+-=?';
validChars = ['A':'Z' 'a':'z' '0':'9' specialChars];
password = blanks(passwordLength);
% Generate random characters for password
for i = 1:<|fim_suf|>,1)) = char(randi([65,90]));
end
for i = 1:numLowercase
 password(randperm(passwordLength,1)) = char(randi([97,122]));
end
for i = 1:numNumbers
 password(randperm(passwordLength,1)) = char(randi([48,57]));
end
for i = 1:numSpecialChars
 password(randperm(passwordLength,1)) = specialChars(randi(length(specialChars)));
end
for i = 1:passwordLength
 if password(i) == ' '
 password(i) = validChars(randi(length(validChars)));
 end
end
% Display password and character frequency table
disp(['Password: ' password])
freqTable = tabulate(password);
disp('Character frequency table:')
disp('Character | Frequency')
disp(freqTable(:,1:2))
```
This code generates a password that is 12 characters long and contains at least two uppercase letters, two lowercase letters, two numbers, and two special characters. It also displays a table showing the frequency of each character type in the generated password. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
