<|user|>
Can you explain the concept of time dilation in physics?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Time dilation is a phenomenon predicted by Einstein's theory of relativity, which states that time appears to move slower for objects traveling at high speeds or in strong gravitational fields. This means that time passes slower for a person on a spaceship traveling near the speed of light than it does for someone on Earth. The effect of time dilation has been observed experimentally and has important implications for space travel and our understanding of the nature of time and space. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


