<|end|>
<|asst|>
There are several common treatments for depression, including antidepressant medication, psychotherapy, and lifestyle changes such as regular exercise and healthy eating habits. Antidepressants work by altering the balance of chemicals in the brain that affect mood, while psychotherapy can help individuals identify and change negative thought patterns and behaviors. Additionally, mindfulness techniques and relaxation exercises, such as meditation or yoga, may also be effective in managing symptoms of depression. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
