Can you explain the concept of quantum entanglement?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Quantum entanglement is a phenomenon that occurs when two or more particles become connected in such a way that the state of one particle is dependent on the state of the other particle, regardless of the distance between them. This means that if one particle is observed to have a certain property, the other particle will instantaneously take on a corresponding property, regardless of how far apart they are. This concept is a fundamental principle of quantum physics and has been demonstrated through numerous experiments. The implications of quantum entanglement are still being explored, but it has potential applications in fields such as cryptography and quantum computing. <|endoftext|>
