How do black holes form and what happens inside them?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Black holes are formed from the remnants of massive stars after they die. When a star runs out of fuel and can no longer produce energy, it collapses in on itself due to gravity, creating an incredibly dense object with a strong gravitational pull. Inside a black hole, the gravitational pull is so strong that not even light can escape, making it impossible to see what's happening inside. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
