1/2 cup of butter
1 teaspoon of baking powder")) <(sort <(echo "1 cup of flour
1 teaspoon of baking soda"))
```

Here, the `-23` option tells the `comm` command to suppress the lines that are common to both files and to output only the lines that are unique to the second file (i.e., recipe B). This gives us the set of ingredients that are in Recipe B but not in Recipe A. <|endoftext|>
