The action of purchasing a new car was performed by Jack, resulting in the ownership of said car. Please rewrite this sentence in the passive voice. Additionally, provide an explanation of the differences between the active and passive voice and examples of when it is appropriate to use each one.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The new car was purchased by Jack, resulting in Jack's ownership of the car.
Active voice is when the subject of the sentence performs the action, while in the passive voice, the subject receives the action. For example, "John ate the pizza" is in the active voice, while "The pizza was eaten by John" is in the passive voice. 
Active voice is usually preferred when the subject is important or when the focus is on the action being performed. Passive voice, on the other hand, is used when the subject is less important or when the focus is on the action being received. It can also be used to avoid assigning blame or responsibility. For example, "Mistakes were made" is a passive construction that avoids directly blaming anyone. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
