Can you explain the difference between deductive and inductive reasoning with examples?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Deductive reasoning starts with a general premise and deduces specific conclusions that must follow. For example, "All men are mortal, Socrates is a man, therefore Socrates is mortal." Inductive reasoning starts with specific observations and infers general conclusions that may be probable but not certain. For example, "Every crow I have seen has been black, therefore all crows are black." <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
