<|end|>
<|asst|>
The internet is a global network of computers and servers that communicate with each other using standardized protocols and languages such as TCP/IP, HTTP, and HTML. When you access a website or send an email, your computer sends a request to a server through your internet service provider (ISP). The server then responds by sending the requested information back to your computer, where it is displayed in your web browser or email client. This process of transmitting data between computers and servers is facilitated by a complex system of routers, switches, and hubs that help to direct traffic across the internet. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


<|fim_mid|>and bats<|fim_eom|>

