<|user|>
How can I modify the C# code you provided to handle a 10-star rating scale instead of a 5-star rating scale?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To modify the C# code to handle a 10-star rating scale instead of a 5-star rating scale, you can simply update the `maxRating` parameter to be 10. Here is the modified code:
```
public static double ConvertTo1StarRating(double rating, double maxRating)
{
 double oneStarRating = 1.0 / maxRating;
 double convertedRating = rating * oneStarRating;
 return Math.Round(convertedRating, 2);
}
// Example usage:
double rating1 = 9.6;
double maxRating1 = 10.0;
double convertedRating1 = ConvertTo1StarRating(rating1, maxRating1); // Returns 0.96
double rating2 = 7.0;
double maxRating2 = 10.0;
double convertedRating2 = ConvertTo1StarRating(rating2, maxRating2); // Returns 0.7
```
As before, you can call the `ConvertTo1StarRating` method with different input ratings and maximum ratings to get the corresponding converted ratings on the 1-star scale. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


