<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you explain what Dolby Vision is and how it relates to the iPhone 12's camera?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Dolby Vision is an HDR (High Dynamic Range) technology that enhances the colors and contrast in video content. The iPhone 12's camera system can record video in Dolby Vision at up to 4K resolution and 60 frames per second. This means that videos recorded on the iPhone 12 can be viewed on compatible devices with brighter highlights, deeper blacks, and a wider range of colors. <|endoftext|>
