<|user|>
Suppose I have four numbers: 12, 16, 18, and 22. I want to calculate their average using a function in MATLAB. How can I do that?
Can you please provide a MATLAB code snippet that defines a function named "calculate_average" which takes four input arguments (num1, num2, num3, num4) and returns the average of these numbers?
The function should be able to handle any four numbers passed to it as arguments.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! Here's a MATLAB code snippet that defines a function named "calculate_average" which takes four input arguments (num1, num2, num3, num4) and returns the average of these numbers:
```
function avg = calculate_average(num1, num2, num3, num4)
 avg = (num1 + num2 + num3 + num4) / 4;
end
```
To use this function with the numbers you provided, you can call it like this:
```
>> calculate_average(12, 16, 18, 22)
ans =
 17
```
This will return the average of the four numbers, which is 17. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
That's great! But what if I have a large set of numbers and I want to calculate their average using MATLAB? Is there any built-in function for that?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, MATLAB has a built-in function called "mean" that can be used to calculate the average of a set of numbers. You can use this function to easily calculate the average of a large set of numbers. Here's an example code snippet:

```
% Define a vector of numbers
numbers = [12, 16, 18, 22, 25, 30, 35, 40];

% Use the mean function to calculate the average
average = mean(numbers);
```

In this example, we have defined a vector of numbers and then used the "mean" function to calculate the average of those numbers. The resulting value is stored in the "average" variable. You can replace the "numbers" vector with your own set of numbers to calculate their average. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Thanks for the explanation! Now suppose I want to plot a sine wave in MATLAB. Can you guide me on how to do that?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, to plot a sine wave in MATLAB, you can use the "plot" function. Here's a sample code that generates a sine wave and plots it:

```
% Define the range of x values
x = 0:0.1:6*pi;

% Calculate the corresponding y values (sine wave)
y = sin(x);

% Plot the sine wave
plot(x, y);

% Add labels to the plot
xlabel('x');
ylabel('sin(x)');
title('Sine Wave');
```

In this code, <|fim_mid|>we first define the range of x values using the colon operator. We then calculate the corresponding y values (sine wave) using the "sin" function. Finally<|fim_eom|>

