<|user|>
Can you explain the difference between git pull and git fetch?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! Both `git pull` and `git fetch` are used to update a local repository with changes from a remote repository. However, there is a key difference between the two.

The `git fetch` command retrieves changes from the remote repository but doesn't merge them into your local branch. It only updates your local copy of the remote branch, allowing you to review the changes before merging them. This is useful when you want to see what has changed in the remote repository before merging it into your local branch.

On the other hand, the `git pull` command not only retrieves the changes from the remote repository but also merges them into your current branch. This means that the changes are immediately reflected in your working directory.

In summary, `git fetch` retrieves the changes from the remote repository without merging them, while `git pull` retrieves the changes and automatically merges them into your current branch. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




