Could you explain the concept of cognitive dissonance?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Cognitive dissonance is the psychological discomfort that arises from holding two or more conflicting beliefs, values, or attitudes. People tend to seek consistency among their beliefs and actions, so when there is a conflict, they may experience feelings of tension or anxiety. To resolve this dissonance, individuals may change their beliefs, behaviors or attitudes to align with each other. The concept of cognitive dissonance has been widely studied in psychology and has significant implications for understanding human decision-making and behavior. <|endoftext|>
