I've heard about concentrated solar power (CSP). How does it differ from traditional photovoltaic (PV) solar panels?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Concentrated solar power (CSP) systems use mirrors or lenses to focus sunlight onto a small area, <|fim_suf|>, turning turbines to generate electricity. While traditional photovoltaic (PV) solar panels convert sunlight directly into electricity using semiconducting materials, CSP requires thermal energy conversion. CSP is better suited for large-scale utility projects where high temperatures can be achieved, whereas PV panels are often used for residential and commercial applications. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
