How did the Industrial Revolution impact society?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The Industrial Revolution had a profound impact on society by transforming the way goods were produced and consumed. It led to the growth of factories and mass production, which made goods more affordable and accessible to people. It also created new jobs and increased economic prosperity, but also had negative effects such as harsh working conditions and environmental degradation. <|endoftext|>
