Surgical masks are also effective in reducing transmission, as they can block large respiratory droplets from reaching others. Cloth masks are less effective than surgical masks, but can still provide some protection. Double masking, or wearing a cloth mask over a surgical mask, has been shown to provide even more protection.

In addition to wearing masks, other preventative measures such as social distancing and frequent handwashing should also be practiced to slow the spread of COVID-19. <|endoftext|>
