Can you provide some notable examples of buttes and mesas in the United States?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Certainly! One well-known example of a butte is Devils Tower in Wyoming, which rises over 800 feet above the surrounding landscape and is famous for its hexagonal columns. Another example is Shiprock in New Mexico, which is a volcanic plug that rises over 1,500 feet above the surrounding desert. 
As for mesas, there are many notable examples across the American Southwest. One of the most famous is the Grand Mesa in Colorado, which is the largest flat-topped mountain in the world and covers an area of over 500 square miles. Another example is Monument Valley in Utah and Arizona, which is known for its iconic sandstone formations that rise hundreds of feet above the surrounding desert floor. <|endoftext|>
