Dance and music are often intertwined, with the movement of the dance being closely linked to the rhythm, tempo, and melody of the music. However, it is possible for one to exist without the other. For example, some contemporary dance performances may utilize silence or non-musical sounds as a way to create tension or emphasize certain movements. Conversely, some forms of music such as classical symphonies may feature dance-like movements or gestures as part of the performance, but not necessarily require physical dancing. Ultimately, the relationship between dance and music can vary widely depending on the context and artistic vision of the performer or choreographer. <|endoftext|>
