Yes, there are quite a few idiomatic phrases that originated in medieval England. One such phrase is "sleep tight," which was coined during that time period due to the fact that mattresses were filled with straw, and ropes would need to be tightened to keep the mattress from sagging. Another phrase is "raining cats and dogs," which came about because animals would often take refuge on thatched roofs during storms, and when it rained heavily, they would fall off. These are just a few examples; there are many more! <|endoftext|>
