Upon further investigation, you discover that the message has been encrypted using a substitution cipher, where each letter has been replaced by another letter. 
After some intense analysis, you notice that the code follows a specific pattern. The first letter of the message corresponds to a letter that is 23 letters after it in the alphabet, the second letter corresponds to a letter that is 10 letters before it in the alphabet, and so on. 
