<|end|>
<|user|>
How efficient are solar panels at converting sunlight into electricity?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The efficiency of solar panels varies depending on several factors, such as the type of panel, its age, and the amount of sunlight it receives. Generally, modern solar panels have an efficiency of around 20%, meaning they can convert about one-fifth of the sunlight that hits them into usable electricity. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What are some advantages of using solar power?
<|end|>
