Here's an example Ruby code that generates a sentence starting with "She had a dream" and includes three unique details about the dream:
```
details = ["in a forest", "with talking animals", "ending with flying"]
sentence = "She had a dream #{details.sample(3).join(', ')}."
puts sentence
```
This code creates an array of three unique dream details, then uses the `sample` method to randomly select three of those details and join them together into a sentence. The resulting sentence will be printed to the console. You can modify the `details` array to include different dream details as needed. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
