Name lesser-known Italian filmmakers who have made a significant impact on the film industry.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here are some lesser-known Italian filmmakers who have made a significant impact on the film industry:
1. Michelangelo Antonioni - known for his art house films, Antonioni is considered one of the most important filmmakers of the 20th century.
2. Federico Fellini - although Fellini is well-known for his films, his name may not be as recognizable to the general public. He is considered one of the greatest Italian filmmakers of all time.
3. Luchino Visconti - Visconti was a pioneer of Italian neorealism and made several critically acclaimed films.
4. Vittorio De Sica - another neorealist filmmaker, De Sica's films often dealt with the struggles of everyday people.
5. Ermanno Olmi - Olmi was known for his realistic and socially conscious films, which often focused on the lives of workers and peasants.
6. Nanni Moretti - Moretti is a contemporary filmmaker who has gained international recognition for his films, which often deal with political and social issues in Italy. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
