Certainly! Here's a sample code that generates two new words from 'flower' and 'bouquet' in C#:
```csharp
using System;
class Program
{
 static void Main(string[] args)
 {
 string flower = "flower";
 string bouquet = "bouquet";
 string delightfulFlower = flower + "ful";
 string delightfulBouquet = "delightful " + bouquet;
 Console.WriteLine("Delightful flower: " + delightfulFlower);
 Console.WriteLine("Delightful bouquet: " + delightfulBouquet);
 }
}
```
This code creates two new words by adding the suffix "ful" to "flower" and the prefix "delightful " to "bouquet". The output will be:
```
Delightful flower: flowerful
Delightful bouquet: delightful bouquet
```
I hope this helps! <|endoftext|>
