Herd immunity refers to a situation where enough people in a population have become immune to a disease, either through vaccination or previous infection, that the disease is no longer able to spread easily within the community. This means that even those who are not immune, <|fim_mid|>such as people who are too young or too sick to be vaccinated<|fim_eom|>

