<|fim_suf|>, we can use memoization to cache the results of subproblems involving smaller substrings of s1 and s2. This can reduce the time complexity from O(m*n) to O(m*n), as we only need to calculate each subproblem once.

To implement memoization, we can use a hash table or an array to store the values of previously calculated subproblems. Before calculating a new subproblem, we can check if its value has already been calculated and stored in the memoization table. If so, we can simply return the cached result instead of recalculating it. <|endoftext|>
