Here's a recipe for an appetizer that meets all the requirements:
Ingredients:
- Edamame (Japan)
- Guacamole (Mexico)
- Prosciutto (Italy)
- Feta cheese (Greece)
- Pomegranate seeds (Iran)
Instructions:
1. Cook the edamame according to package instructions and set aside to cool.
2. In a small bowl, mix together the guacamole and crumbled feta cheese.
3. Take a slice of prosciutto and spread a thin layer of the guacamole mixture on top.
4. Place a small spoonful of edamame on top of the guacamole mixture.
5. Sprinkle a few pomegranate seeds on top of the edamame.
6. Roll up the prosciutto tightly, tucking in the edges as you go.
7. Cut the rolled prosciutto into bite-sized pieces and serve on a platter.
To visually present the dish, arrange the bite-sized pieces in a circular pattern on a white or black platter, with a small bowl of extra pomegranate seeds in the center.
