How do scientists estimate the age of fossils?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Scientists use a variety of methods to estimate the age of fossils. One common method is radiometric dating, which involves measuring the decay of radioactive isotopes in the fossil over time. By comparing the ratio of isotopes in the fossil to the ratio of isotopes in the surrounding rock or sediment, <|fim_mid|>scientists can determine how long ago the fossil was formed.

Another method is stratigraphy<|fim_eom|>

