Certainly! To check if a list is in ascending order, we simply need to ensure that each number in the list is greater than or equal to the number before it. In this case, each successive number is larger than the previous one, so the list is indeed in ascending order. As for checking if the numbers are prime, we look at each number in turn and check whether it is only divisible by itself and 1. For all the numbers in your list, this is true, so we can conclude that they are prime. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
That makes sense. How can we determine if a larger list of numbers is in ascending order and contains only prime numbers?
