The process is the same for a larger list. We would check that each successive number is greater than or equal to the previous one, and then check each number in turn to see if it is prime. However, this can become quite tedious for very long lists. One possible shortcut is to use a computer program or an online tool that specializes in checking for prime numbers. This way, we can quickly determine if each number in the list is prime, without having to manually check them all ourselves. <|endoftext|>
