How can I avoid cross-contamination when cooking in the kitchen?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To avoid cross-contamination when cooking in the kitchen, you should: 
1. Use separate cutting boards for raw meat and produce 
2. Wash your hands frequently 
3. Clean utensils and surfaces thoroughly between uses 
4. Store raw meat on the bottom shelf of the fridge to prevent juices from dripping onto other foods 
5. Cook meat to the appropriate temperature to kill bacteria <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
