2. Airport attributes: Other airport attributes such as parking facilities or lounge access can be added to the "airports" field to provide more information for customers when selecting their flights. This will help customers choose airports that offer the facilities they need.
3. Reviews: Reviews from other customers who have flown on the same airline or through the same airport can be added to the JSON data. This will help customers get a better understanding of the quality of service and facilities offered by the airline or airport.
4. Flight status updates: The JSON data can be updated in real-time with flight status updates. This will help customers stay informed about any delays or cancellations and plan accordingly.
Overall, by providing more information and updates, the JSON data can help customers make informed decisions and improve their overall experience during air ticket bookings. <|endoftext|>
