<|fim_suf|>, it's a bit 'stranger than fiction'. Here's the catch: each number in the table is actually a concatenation of two smaller numbers. For example, '12' is made up of '1' and '2'. Using this logic, we can split each number in the table and reorganize them into pairs:
|  |  |  |  |  |  |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 |
| 7 | 8 | 9 | 1 | 0 | 1 |
| 1 | 3 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 5 |
Now, notice that each pair of numbers adds up to '9', except for the missing pair in the bottom row. It turns out that the missing pair is '1' and '8', which adds up to '9'. Thus, the missing number is '1718'. Can you use HTML and JavaScript to replicate this puzzle and solution on your own website?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, I can help you create a similar puzzle and solution on your website using HTML and JavaScript. Here's an example code:
HTML:
```
|  |  |  |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 25 | 36 | 47 |
| 58 | 69 | 71 |
| 82 | 93 | __ |
Find Missing Number

```
JavaScript:
```
function findMissingNumber() {
 // Get all the table cells
 var cells = document.getElementsByTagName("td");
 // Create an array to store each digit of the numbers
 var digits = [];
 // Loop through each cell and split the numbers into digits
 for (var i = 0; i < cells.length; i++) {
 var num = cells[i].innerHTML;
 digits.push(num.charAt(0));
 digits.push(num.charAt(1));
 }
 // Loop through each pair of digits and add them up
 var sum = 0;
 for (var j = 0; j < digits.length; j += 2) {
 var pairSum = parseInt(digits[j]) + parseInt(digits[j+1]);
 // Check if the pair sum is not 9
 if (pairSum !== 9) {
 // Calculate the missing pair and update the result
 var missingPair = 9 - pairSum;
 var missingNumber = missingPair.toString() + (9 - missingPair).toString();
 document.getElementById("result").innerHTML = "The missing number is " + missingNumber;
 return;
 }
 }
}
```
This JavaScript function will extract all the digits from the table cells, calculate the sum of each pair of digits, and find the missing pair that adds up to 9. Then, it will update the result paragraph with the missing number. You can customize the table values and IDs to create your own puzzle. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
