Can you discuss the symbolism behind the design and construction of the Washington Monument?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The Washington Monument was intended to serve as a symbol of America's founding father, George Washington. The monument's design is inspired by ancient Egyptian obelisks, which were seen as symbols of stability and eternal life. The choice of building material was also symbolic; the monument is constructed from white marble blocks, which represent purity and virtue. Additionally, the cornerstone of the monument bears the inscription "Laid on Bed of Foundation Stone on Which the Sepulcher of Jesus Rests," indicating the monument's connection to Christian tradition. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
