Yes, to modify the code to only generate uppercase letters, we can simply remove the lowercase letters from the `$characters` variable. Here's the updated code:
```
php
$characters = '0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ';
$string = '';
for ($i = 0; $i < 10; $i++) {
 $string .= $characters[rand(0, strlen($characters) - 1)];
}
echo $string;
?
```
As you can see, we have removed the `abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz` portion of the `$characters` variable. Now, only uppercase letters and numbers will be used to generate the random string. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
