php
$characters = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ';
$string = '';
for ($i = 0; $i < 10; $i++) {
 $string .= $characters[rand(0, strlen($characters) - 1)];
}
echo $string;
?
```
As you can see, we have removed the `0123456789` portion of the `$characters` variable and added both uppercase and lowercase letters. Now, only letters will be used to generate the random string, with a mix of uppercase and lowercase letters included. <|endoftext|>
