<|user|>
Can you explain the concept of recursion in computer programming?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Recursion is a programming technique where a function calls itself from within its own code. It involves breaking down a problem into smaller subproblems and then solving each subproblem by recursively calling the same function until a base case is reached. The base case is the point at which the function stops calling itself to avoid an infinite loop. Recursion can be used to solve problems that have a recursive structure, such as traversing trees or searching through graphs. However, it can also lead to performance issues if not implemented carefully. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




