Apple pies quickly gained popularity in the United States due to the abundance of apple orchards and the versatility of the fruit. Apple pies became an iconic American dessert often served during holidays and special occasions such as Thanksgiving and Fourth of July.

The popularity of apple pies can also be attributed to its simplicity in ingredients and preparation, making it a popular dish for home cooks and bakers alike.

