Speaking of animal behavior, can animals really sense earthquakes before they happen? How do they do it?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
It is a popular belief that animals can sense an impending earthquake before it happens. Some studies suggest that this may be due to their ability to detect changes in the earth's magnetic field or the release of gases that occur before an earthquake. Others believe that animals may be able to sense subtle changes in the environment, such as changes in atmospheric pressure, that occur before an earthquake. However, more research is needed to fully understand how animals are able to detect earthquakes and whether they can reliably predict them. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
