That's great, thank you for explaining it so clearly! I have another question related to lines. Can you explain the difference between a horizontal line and a vertical line?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! A horizontal line is a line that goes from left to right or right to left, parallel to the x-axis, and has a slope of 0. The equation of a horizontal line is y = b, where b is a constant value. On the other hand, a vertical line is a line that goes from up to down or down to up, parallel to the y-axis, and has an undefined slope. The equation of a vertical line is x = a, where a is a constant value. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
