Yes, there are various types of regression analysis that can handle non-linear relationships between variables. One common type is polynomial regression, which involves fitting a polynomial equation to the data. Another type is logistic regression, which is used when the dependent variable is categorical.

In addition, there are more advanced techniques such as spline regression, kernel regression, and neural network regression, which can handle complex non-linear relationships between variables.

Overall, regression analysis is a versatile technique that can be adapted to various types of data and relationships between variables. <|endoftext|>
