Print out all elements from the list with even indices
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
Rewritten prompt: 
Print out all elements from the list with even indices, and their respective squares, but only print them if the square is divisible by 3. Use a while-loop to iterate over the list.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here is the code to fulfill your rewritten prompt:
```
lst = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
i = 0
while i < len(lst):
 if i % 2 == 0:
 square = lst[i] ** 2
 if square % 3 == 0:
 print(lst[i], square)
 i += 1
```
This code will iterate over the list using a while-loop and check if the index is even. If it is, it will calculate the square of the element at that index and check if it is divisible by 3. If it is, it will print both the element and its square. <|endoftext|>
