Yes please. Can you recommend alternative ingredients that would be suitable for people with gluten allergies or intolerances?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
For people with gluten allergies or intolerances, you could replace the wheat flour in the recipe with a gluten-free flour blend made from rice flour, tapioca starch, and potato starch. You could also add xanthan gum or guar gum to help bind the dough together, since gluten provides the structure and elasticity in baked goods. Additionally, you could use gluten-free oats instead of wheat-based oats, and ensure that all other ingredients are certified gluten-free to avoid cross-contamination. These substitutions should produce a similar taste and texture in the final product, while making it safe for people with gluten sensitivities to enjoy. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


