<|asst|>
The phrase that implies that money is a powerful force that can affect decisions or actions is "Money talks". This phrase means that money has the power to influence people and their actions.
The commonly used expression is "Money doesn't grow on trees". This phrase is used to convey the idea that money is not easy to come by and that one should be careful with their spending. 
The other phrases and their meanings are:
- "Cash is king": This phrase means that cash is the most valuable form of payment and is preferred over other forms of payment.
- "You gotta pay to play": This phrase means that in order to participate or be successful in something, one must be willing to invest time, effort, or money.
- "He who pays the piper calls the tune": This phrase means that the person who provides the money for something has the right to determine how it is done.
- "A fool and his money are soon parted": This phrase means that people who are not careful with their money will quickly lose it. <|endoftext|>
