<|user|>
Can you explain the concept of opportunity cost and give an example of it?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Opportunity cost is the value of the next best alternative forgone when making a decision. In other words, it is the cost of what one must give up in order to pursue a certain action or decision.

For example, imagine you have $10 and you are trying to decide whether to spend it on a movie ticket or a pizza. If you choose to buy the movie ticket, your opportunity cost would be the pizza you could have bought instead. On the other hand, <|fim_suf|>, your opportunity cost would be the movie ticket you could have seen instead. In both cases, the opportunity cost is the value of the foregone alternative.

Opportunity cost is important to consider when making decisions because it helps us weigh the benefits and costs of each option and choose the most valuable one. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


