How does electricity work in terms of atoms and electrons?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Electricity is the flow of electric charge, typically carried by electrons. Atoms consist of a central nucleus made up of protons and neutrons, surrounded by a cloud of electrons. When electrons flow through a conductor, such as a copper wire, they move from atom to atom by jumping from one energy level to another. This movement of electrons creates an electric current, which can be used to power electrical devices. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
