<|user|>
How can I convert the following positive assertion about the current state of the sky's illumination into a statement that describes a lack of that illumination in C#?
bool isSkyIlluminated = true;
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can convert the positive assertion into a statement that describes a lack of sky illumination in C# by using the logical NOT operator. Here's an example:
bool isSkyDark = !isSkyIlluminated;
This will assign the value of "false" to the variable "isSkyDark", indicating that the sky is not illuminated. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you explain the concept of inheritance in object-oriented programming?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Inheritance is a fundamental concept in object-oriented programming that allows you to create new classes based on existing ones. With inheritance, you can create a new class which inherits all the data members and member functions from an existing class, known as the base or parent class. The new class, known as the derived or child class, <|fim_mid|>can then add new data members and member functions<|fim_eom|>

<|fim_suf|>}
