What is the verb phrase in the sentence "We had to be there before noon" using part-of-speech tagging approach in Python?
You can use the Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK) library in Python and the following formula to extract the verb phrase:
```
import nltk
sentence = "We had to be there before noon"
tokens = nltk.word_tokenize(sentence)
tags = nltk.pos_tag(tokens)
grammar = "VP: {??}"
cp = nltk.RegexpParser(grammar)
result = cp.parse(tags)
for subtree in result.subtrees():
 if subtree.label() == "VP":
 print(subtree)
```
This will output the verb phrase "had to be" in the sentence.
