How can I retrieve data from an XML file using Xpath expressions in Python?
Assuming you have an XML file named "data.xml" with the following structure:
John
25
New York
Jane
30
Los Angeles
You can use the following Python code to retrieve the value of the "name" element for the first "person" node:
import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
tree = ET.parse('data.xml')
root = tree.getroot()
name = root.find('person[1]/name').text
print(name)
This code uses the ElementTree module to parse the XML file and retrieve the root element. The Xpath expression "person[1]/name" is used to select the first "person" node and retrieve its "name" element. The text value of the element is then printed to the console.
