<|user|>
What is the proper way to create a survey form in Go code that asks for the following information to help a branding expert suggest suitable business names for your graphic design studio in an Excel table?
- Mission statement of your graphic design studio
- Target audience
- Unique services or specialties that your studio offers
- Values that your business holds
Please provide the necessary Go code to create this survey form.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's an example Go code to create a survey form that asks for the information you mentioned:
```go
package main
import (
 "fmt"
 "os"
)
func main() {
 // Create an Excel table to store the survey results
 file, err := os.Create("survey.xlsx")
 if err != nil {
 panic(err)
 }
 defer file.Close()
 // Create a new sheet in the Excel table to store the survey data
 sheet, err := file.AddSheet("Survey Results")
 if err != nil {
 panic(err)
 }
 // Add column headers to the sheet
 row := sheet.AddRow()
 row.AddCell().SetValue("Mission Statement")
 row.AddCell().SetValue("Target Audience")
 row.AddCell().SetValue("Unique Services")
 row.AddCell().SetValue("Values")
 // Ask the user for the survey information
 var missionStatement string
 fmt.Print("What is the mission statement of your graphic design studio? ")
 fmt.Scanln(&missionStatement)
 var targetAudience string
 fmt.Print("Who is your target audience? ")
 fmt.Scanln(&targetAudience)
 var uniqueServices string
 fmt.Print("What unique services or specialties does your studio offer? ")
 fmt.Scanln(&uniqueServices)
 var values string
 fmt.Print("What values does your business hold? ")
 fmt.Scanln(&values)
 // Add the survey data to the Excel table
 row = sheet.AddRow()
 row.AddCell().SetValue(missionStatement)
 row.AddCell().SetValue(targetAudience)
 row.AddCell().SetValue(uniqueServices)
 row.AddCell().SetValue(values)
 // Save the Excel table
 err = file.Save("survey.xlsx")
 if err != nil {
 panic(err)
 }
 fmt.Println("Thank you for completing the survey!")
}
```
This code uses the `github.com/tealeg/xlsx` package to create an Excel table and add survey data to it. When the user runs the program, they will be prompted to enter the survey information, which will be added to the Excel table. The table will be saved to a file named "survey.xlsx" in the current directory. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
