<|end|>
<|user|>
What are the differences between reinforcement learning and supervised learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Reinforcement learning differs from supervised learning in that there is no specific target output for the algorithm to learn. Instead, the algorithm learns by trial and error through interacting with an environment and receiving feedback in the form of rewards or penalties. Supervised learning, on the other hand, has a specific target output that the algorithm tries to match. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


