Can you explain the concept of entropy?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Entropy is a measure of the degree of disorder or randomness in a system. It is also a measure of the amount of energy that is unavailable in a closed system to do useful work. The second law of thermodynamics states that the total entropy of a closed system always increases over time, which means that the energy in the system becomes more dispersed and less available for useful work. This is why machines are not 100% efficient since some energy is always lost to entropy. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


