What is the difference between OLED and LCD displays? Which one is better?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
OLED displays use organic compounds to emit light when an electric current is passed through them, while LCD displays use a backlight to illuminate liquid crystals. OLED displays offer better contrast and deeper blacks since each pixel can be individually turned off, while LCD displays have a brighter overall brightness and are more power-efficient. Both technologies have their advantages and disadvantages, and which one is better depends on the specific use case. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
