A simple machine is a device that makes work easier by reducing the force required to perform a task or changing the direction of the applied force. Examples of simple machines include levers, pulleys, wedges, screws, wheels and axles, and inclined planes. These machines work based on basic principles of physics, such as the conservation of energy and the transfer of force, to accomplish tasks that would otherwise require more effort or be impossible to perform. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How do simple machines make work easier?
<|end|>
