Can you explain the concept of natural selection in evolution?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Natural selection is a process by which certain traits become more or less common in populations over time. Organisms with advantageous traits are more likely to survive and reproduce, passing on those traits to their offspring. Over long periods of time, this can lead to significant changes in the characteristics of a population, ultimately resulting in the formation of new species. <|endoftext|>
