Can you explain the concept of cognitive dissonance?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Cognitive dissonance is a mental state in which a person holds two or more conflicting beliefs, values, or ideas. This creates discomfort or tension and may lead the person to alter their beliefs or behaviors in order to reduce the dissonance. For example, a smoker may experience cognitive dissonance if they believe smoking is unhealthy but continue to smoke. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Is there any difference between empathy and sympathy?
