textbf{Differences between AI, Machine Learning, and Deep Learning:}
Artificial Intelligence (AI) is an umbrella term that encompasses various techniques that enable computer systems to perform tasks that typically require human-level intelligence. Machine Learning (ML), a subset of AI, involves using algorithms that learn from data to make predictions or decisions without being explicitly programmed. Deep Learning (DL), another subset of AI, uses artificial neural networks to extract features from data and make more complex decisions.

