List 4 facts about polar bears
<|end|>
<|asst|>
1. Polar bears are excellent swimmers and are known to swim long distances across open water.
2. They have a thick layer of blubber, which helps to keep them warm in the freezing Arctic temperatures.
3. Adult male polar bears can weigh up to 1,500 pounds, making them the largest land predator in the world.
4. Polar bears have a keen sense of smell and are able to detect seals, <|fim_mid|>their main prey<|fim_eom|>

