<|user|>
What is the history behind the FedEx logo?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The original FedEx logo was created in 1971 by Lindon Leader while he was working at the design firm, <|fim_suf|>, speed, and innovation. The hidden arrow in the negative space between the "E" and the "x" represents the company's forward momentum and transportation capabilities. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How has the FedEx logo changed over time?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Over the years, the FedEx logo has undergone several changes. In 1994, the logo was updated to give it a more modern look with a bolder font and a more streamlined arrow. In 2000, the logo was simplified even further, with the removal of the word "Express" and the abbreviation of the company name to just "FedEx." In 2016, the logo underwent its most recent update, with a new sans-serif font and a slightly modified arrow. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Are there any other logos that have hidden meanings like the FedEx logo?
<|end|>
