<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! A sole proprietorship is a business that is owned by one person, who is personally responsible for all debts and liabilities of the business. A partnership is similar to a sole proprietorship, but it involves two or more people sharing ownership of the business. Limited liability company (LLC) is a hybrid entity that provides the limited liability protection of a corporation while retaining the tax benefits of a partnership. A corporation is a separate legal entity from its owners, shareholders have limited liability, and the corporation can issue stocks to raise funds. <|endoftext|>
