<|user|>
How do scientists determine the structure of fluorescent proteins?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Scientists determine the structure of fluorescent proteins using a variety of techniques, including X-ray crystallography, NMR spectroscopy, and cryo-EM. These techniques allow researchers to determine the three-dimensional arrangement of atoms within the protein, which can provide insight into its function and mechanism. For example, determining the structure of green fluorescent protein (GFP) led to the development of numerous applications in cell biology and biotechnology, including the visualization of subcellular structures and the tracking of protein localization and movement in living cells. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


