<|user|>
How can I use Shell cmd to download a large file from a remote server while ensuring data integrity? Can you provide a sample code that can download the file using curl command with checksum verification?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, you can use the `curl` command with checksum verification to download a large file from a remote server while ensuring data integrity. Here is a sample code:
```
curl -O -C - https://example.com/largefile.tar.gz
curl -O https://example.com/largefile.tar.gz.sha256
sha256sum -c largefile.tar.gz.sha256
```
In the above code, the `-O` option tells `curl` to write the output to a file with the same name as the remote file. The `-C -` option tells `curl` to resume the download from where it left off if the download is interrupted. The `https://example.com/largefile.tar.gz.sha256` is the file containing the SHA-256 checksum of the remote file. The `sha256sum -c largefile.tar.gz.sha256` command verifies the checksum of the downloaded file.
You can replace `https://example.com/largefile.tar.gz` with the actual URL of the remote file you want to download, <|fim_mid|>and `largefile.tar.gz.sha256` with the actual name of the checksum file. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
