<|fim_suf|>, if we know that all men are mortal, and that Socrates is a man, then deductive reasoning would allow us to conclude that Socrates is mortal. On the other hand, if we observe that multiple crows are black, inductive reasoning would lead us to conclude that all crows are likely to be black. <|endoftext|>
