<|end|>
<|asst|>
Entropy is a measure of the amount of disorder or randomness in a system. In thermodynamics, it is a fundamental property that describes the energy unavailable for work in a thermodynamic process. It increases in any spontaneous process and can never decrease. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How does DNA replication occur?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
DNA replication is a process by which the genetic information stored in DNA is copied to produce two identical copies of the original DNA molecule. It involves the unwinding of the double helix, separation of the two strands, and the synthesis of new complementary strands by adding nucleotides according to base-pairing rules. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
