Can you explain what the Higgs boson is and why its discovery was significant?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The Higgs boson is a subatomic particle that was hypothesized to exist as part of the mechanism that gives particles mass. Its discovery was significant because it confirmed the existence of the Higgs field, which is responsible for this mechanism. This discovery completed the Standard Model of particle physics and provided evidence for the validity of the theory of electroweak symmetry breaking. <|endoftext|>
